WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:17.479
"At least my laptop still works," Mr.

2
00:00:17.539 --> 00:00:23.203
Robbins said, even though he couldn't close his computer anymore because of the big dent from the crash.

3
00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.865
"I'm so sorry, Dad," Brooklyn said.

4
00:00:26.885 --> 00:00:28.666
"It was an accident."

5
00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:33.277
Her father nodded, but Brooklyn could tell he was still upset.

6
00:00:33.297 --> 00:00:36.238
"Dirk is right," Brooklyn thought.

7
00:00:36.258 --> 00:00:41.499
"I am a klutz—probably the clumsiest person in the whole world."

8
00:00:42.919 --> 00:00:47.701
At the next Whales practice, Brooklyn tried to keep her coaching tips for the players as quiet as

9
00:00:47.761 --> 00:00:53.422
possible. She made suggestions directly to Marv instead, and he took many of them.

10
00:00:54.423 --> 00:01:00.813
A few times Brooklyn noticed Jacey and other players rolling their eyes after Marv mentioned that Brooklyn had

11
00:01:00.833 --> 00:01:02.353
been the one to suggest something.

12
00:01:03.253 --> 00:01:05.594
Marv had noticed the players' responses too.

13
00:01:05.614 --> 00:01:12.016
"Coaches often have to put the team ahead of their own hurt feelings," he said quietly to Brooklyn.

14
00:01:12.036 --> 00:01:14.877
"You need thick skin to be a coach."

15
00:01:15.497 --> 00:01:17.657
Brooklyn knew the older coach was right.

16
00:01:18.658 --> 00:01:24.779
So at practice she started pretending there was dense fog in the gym and thick cotton in her

17
00:01:24.899 --> 00:01:30.434
ears. That way players' sour looks and unkind words couldn't reach her.

18
00:01:32.035 --> 00:01:37.958
Still, during the team warm-ups before Thursday's game, it was hard to ignore a player from the other

19
00:01:37.998 --> 00:01:43.561
team. She burst into laughter when Brooklyn stumbled over some practice balls.

20
00:01:48.684 --> 00:01:49.624
you a player?"

21
00:01:50.165 --> 00:01:52.186
the tall girl from the Bobcats asked.

22
00:01:52.206 --> 00:01:54.507
"I'm the Whales' team manager."

23
00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:56.148
Brooklyn cleared her throat.

24
00:01:57.092 --> 00:01:59.493
"I'm also the assistant coach."

25
00:01:59.513 --> 00:02:02.554
"Assistant Coach Klutz!"

26
00:02:04.414 --> 00:02:07.795
The girl smirked and ran back onto the court to her teammates.

27
00:02:08.635 --> 00:02:11.876
Brooklyn shook her head and focused on her team's warm-ups.

28
00:02:12.416 --> 00:02:18.218
The ball bounced and flew from Jacey to Aaron to Stuart and around the whole roster of players.

29
00:02:21.619 --> 00:02:24.460
Suddenly Brooklyn realized a player was missing.

30
00:02:25.172 --> 00:02:27.514
She ran down the sideline to the gym office.

31
00:02:29.755 --> 00:02:31.677
She knocked and swung open the door.

32
00:02:35.339 --> 00:02:36.780
It banged into someone.

33
00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:41.383
"Ow!" It was the Bobcats' head coach.

34
00:02:41.403 --> 00:02:43.464
"Oops, sorry, sir!"

35
00:02:43.945 --> 00:02:44.645
Brooklyn said.

36
00:02:45.546 --> 00:02:47.327
The Bobcats' coach rubbed his arm.

37
00:02:47.347 --> 00:02:50.950
"I'm fine, I think."

38
00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.330
"Hi, Brooklyn.

39
00:02:52.551 --> 00:02:55.236
We're exchanging rosters for the game," Marv said.

40
00:02:55.256 --> 00:02:58.017
"Coach Teagan usually does this part.

41
00:02:58.637 --> 00:02:59.938
Are warm-ups going okay?"

42
00:02:59.958 --> 00:03:06.379
"Yep, but She wasn't sure if she should ask this question in front of the other coach.

43
00:03:06.399 --> 00:03:08.220
"Have you seen Dirk?"

44
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.261
Marv's eyes widened.

45
00:03:10.281 --> 00:03:12.501
"He's not out there warming up?"

46
00:03:13.161 --> 00:03:14.362
Brooklyn shook her head.

47
00:03:15.622 --> 00:03:18.843
Marv and the Bobcats' coach looked at the clock over the desk.

48
00:03:19.483 --> 00:03:21.524
Dirk had about three minutes to arrive.

49
00:03:22.632 --> 00:03:25.833
Once the game began, no players could be added to the roster.

50
00:03:25.853 --> 00:03:28.054
"Dirk! You're here!"

51
00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:30.114
Jacey squealed from the court.

52
00:03:30.854 --> 00:03:31.354
"Never mind!

53
00:03:31.755 --> 00:03:33.755
Sounds like he's here," Brooklyn said.

54
00:03:36.856 --> 00:03:39.657
She walked back to the court, with the two men following.

55
00:03:39.677 --> 00:03:46.159
"I wonder if Marv will let Dirk play," she thought.

56
00:03:46.179 --> 00:03:48.639
"He missed all of warm-ups."

57
00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.546
Marv walked up to Dirk, who was tightening the laces on his sneakers.

58
00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:57.188
"You're late, Dirk."

59
00:03:57.208 --> 00:04:02.192
"I'm only here, Marv, because Coach Teagan said I should respect the team."

60
00:04:03.253 --> 00:04:03.873
He stood up.

61
00:04:03.893 --> 00:04:09.717
"I love the Whales, but I don't like that Brooklyn is trying to take over coaching."

62
00:04:10.638 --> 00:04:11.879
Brooklyn stepped closer.

63
00:04:11.899 --> 00:04:15.001
"I'm not trying to take over coaching, Dirk.

64
00:04:15.481 --> 00:04:16.482
I'm helping Marv.

65
00:04:17.063 --> 00:04:18.744
That's what Coach wanted me to do."

66
00:04:20.012 --> 00:04:21.693
Dirk didn't even look at her.

67
00:04:21.713 --> 00:04:28.337
"I'll play for you, Marv, but I won't do Brooklyn's goofy plays, including that girly loop play."

68
00:04:29.277 --> 00:04:30.898
Brooklyn pressed her lips together.

69
00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:33.399
Marv's voice was angry.

70
00:04:33.419 --> 00:04:36.461
"The Whales work and play together, Dirk.

71
00:04:37.061 --> 00:04:40.163
You're part of this team and that means doing what's asked of you.

72
00:04:41.023 --> 00:04:44.185
And remember, Brooklyn is part of this team too."

73
00:04:45.146 --> 00:04:46.426
Brooklyn just stood there.

74
00:04:47.727 --> 00:04:51.417
She wasn't sure whether to say something or just let Marv handle it.

75
00:04:52.098 --> 00:04:54.660
Didn't Dirk know that she loved the team too?

76
00:04:57.361 --> 00:04:58.402
The buzzer sounded.

77
00:04:58.923 --> 00:05:00.524
It was time to start the game.

78
00:05:02.365 --> 00:05:05.487
In the first quarter, Dirk barely moved around the court.

79
00:05:10.331 --> 00:05:11.571
Marv shouted at him.

80
00:05:11.591 --> 00:05:14.413
"Do you want the Whales to lose, Dirk?"

81
00:05:15.654 --> 00:05:20.074
It was clear to Brooklyn and everyone else that Dirk's heart wasn't in the game.

82
00:05:21.035 --> 00:05:24.798
At halftime Marv spoke to Dirk in a low, stern voice.

83
00:05:24.818 --> 00:05:26.500
"Make up your mind.

84
00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:30.263
If you want to be on this team, you have to play with the team.

85
00:05:31.244 --> 00:05:34.927
And don't forget that if we lose today, our season is over."

86
00:05:35.928 --> 00:05:40.052
Then Marv turned to the other players, trying to boost them with the team cheer.

87
00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:41.893
"Whales Whoosh!"

88
00:05:42.814 --> 00:05:47.970
Brooklyn kept her distance from Dirk, not bothering to speak to him or mention him to Marv.

89
00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:51.512
But a few seconds into the second half, she gasped.

90
00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:56.675
Dirk had just let a Bobcat player steal the ball!

91
00:05:58.836 --> 00:06:03.718
She leaned in to Marv and whispered, "Dirk might be trying to make us lose!"

92
00:06:04.679 --> 00:06:06.020
Marv clenched his jaw.

93
00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:07.661
"I hope you're wrong.

94
00:06:08.201 --> 00:06:09.462
I've got my eye on him."

95
00:06:10.542 --> 00:06:21.690
Then, in the final quarter, Dirk made a shot—one that flew through the Bobcats' net, giving the Bobcats

96
00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:22.370
the lead.

97
00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:24.951
Marv quickly called a time-out.

98
00:06:27.152 --> 00:06:28.793
"Stuart, you're in for Dirk."

99
00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:31.134
"What are you doing, Marv?

100
00:06:31.554 --> 00:06:33.235
Dirk's shot was an accident!"

101
00:06:33.635 --> 00:06:34.315
Jacey said.

102
00:06:34.335 --> 00:06:35.976
"We need Dirk!"

103
00:06:35.996 --> 00:06:40.337
"I forgot that we switched nets at the half," Dirk mumbled.

104
00:06:41.058 --> 00:06:42.318
Marv pointed to the bench.

105
00:06:43.098 --> 00:06:45.940
Dirk dropped down and draped a towel over his head.

106
00:06:48.396 --> 00:06:50.397
Brooklyn cheered on the team with Marv.

107
00:06:51.798 --> 00:06:57.202
In the final seconds, Stuart made a shot that put the Whales one point ahead of the Bobcats.

108
00:07:01.424 --> 00:07:04.706
She glanced over to see Dirk peeking out from under his towel.

109
00:07:06.107 --> 00:07:11.891
Maybe he didn't want to do Brooklyn's plays, but he looked happy when the final buzzer sounded and

110
00:07:11.951 --> 00:07:14.012
his team won by one point.

111
00:07:18.128 --> 00:07:20.489
After the game Brooklyn gathered up equipment.

112
00:07:22.751 --> 00:07:25.232
She saw Marv and Dirk talking in the office.

113
00:07:25.972 --> 00:07:31.235
When they came out, Marv gave everyone a quick talk about teamwork and getting ready to face the

114
00:07:31.275 --> 00:07:32.136
Terriers again.

115
00:07:33.297 --> 00:07:36.098
Then the players started packing up and leaving.

116
00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.961
Marv went back to the office.

117
00:07:42.682 --> 00:07:46.464
The only students left in the gym were Dirk, Stuart, and Brooklyn.

118
00:07:47.948 --> 00:07:50.309
"Great job today, Stuart," Brooklyn said.

119
00:07:50.329 --> 00:07:55.451
"You too, Coach Brooklyn," Stuart said, smiling and waving good-bye.

120
00:07:55.471 --> 00:07:57.832
"Hey, Dirk," she called.

121
00:07:58.392 --> 00:08:00.833
He didn't look up, so Brooklyn spoke louder.

122
00:08:00.853 --> 00:08:04.655
"It's okay if you're mad at me, but don't take it out on the team.

123
00:08:05.715 --> 00:08:08.216
The Whales need you to become league champions."

124
00:08:09.157 --> 00:08:12.038
Dirk kept moving to the exit, ignoring her.

125
00:08:14.959 --> 00:08:16.620
But Brooklyn knew he'd heard her.

126
00:08:17.752 --> 00:08:20.713
Brooklyn found her bag and then searched for her phone.

127
00:08:22.074 --> 00:08:26.375
She had one new text: Girls can't coach.

128
00:08:27.175 --> 00:08:28.856
Especially oafs like
